BEHAVIOR string-pack

DESCRIPTION
  Writes a length-prefixed string image ([len:8-byte LE][content]) of the first
  len bytes of src into the caller-owned buffer buf. The leaf half of
  bytes-to-string: buf must outlive any string handle pointing at it, so the
  caller owns it (e.g. pattern MEMORY). buf needs len+8 bytes.

CONTRACT
  INPUT src bytes 65536
  INPUT len int 8
  INPUT buf bytes 65544

HASH 4bb1e8d7

IMPLEMENTATION
  lv = LOAD len 8
  STORE buf lv 8 0
  i = 0
  LABEL loop
    d = IGE i lv 8
    BRANCH d done body
  LABEL body
    b = LOAD src 1 i
    b = AND b 255 8
    off = IADD i 8 8
    STORE buf b 1 off
    i = IADD i 1 8
    JUMP loop
  LABEL done
END
